Acceptance criteria:
  One included actual workstream maps to one repository issue and one issue-containing Project
  item. The primary view is Kanban, with columns grouped by the real Status field.
  All eight fields, task/evidence history and historical dates are preserved; tracking metadata
  cannot create a feedback loop. Local completion is not publication or human acceptance.
  A repeated pilot creates no duplicate issue/item or needless issue-content changes.
  Human edits and uncertain partial operations stop the affected item; independent work may
  continue. Failed reads are errors, never empty inventories.
  Navigation/index and perpetual ledger are excluded. Private documentary/persona work has no
  approved public projection and is excluded pending a separate publication decision.
  Credentials stay in the shared external runner's child environment, never source/payloads.
  No product features, commits/pushes, workflows/dispatch, schedules, releases or remote secrets.

